  "prompt_text": "The figure is a conceptual summary linking several quantum systems through a common interaction picture. At the center, a triangular region labeled “Quantum interactions” shows a free electron interacting with a localized emitter or optical mode between two resonator-like structures. This central coupling is identified with the Jaynes–Cummings model, suggesting that very different physical platforms can be described by the same basic light–matter interaction framework.\n\nAround this center, three simplified quantum objects are compared. One box shows a quantum two-level system, drawn as an emitter with states that can be raised and lowered by Pauli-type operators. Another shows a quantum harmonic oscillator, represented as a photon mode with evenly spaced ladder states and creation/annihilation operators. A third shows a quantum rotor associated with a free electron, also depicted with ladder-like transitions between energy states.\n\nThe side labels indicate two application areas: free-electron–bound-electron resonant interactions on one side and quantum PINEM on the other. Overall, the message is that free electrons, atomic-like emitters, and quantized photonic modes can all be treated within a unified quantum formalism, with analogous state ladders and exchange processes connecting them.",
